TITLE:: FxChain
summary:: a series of effects on a bus, in place, in order
categories:: Libraries>ParaEQ
related:: Classes/FxUnit, Classes/ParaEQ, Classes/Compressor, Classes/FxChainGUI, Classes/FxChainPanel, Classes/ServerPanel

DESCRIPTION::
One group on the server, a list of link::Classes/FxUnit::s inside it, all
working on the same bus one after another. The one everybody wants is the master
chain - an eq and a compressor on the main out - and that is what
link::Classes/ServerPanel::'s code::fx:: section opens:

code::
c = FxChain.master;              // bus 0, every output channel
c.units;                         // -> [ParaEQ, Compressor] when Compressor is installed
c.eq.enabled = true;
c.eq.preset = \warm;
c.compressor.threshold = -18;
c.gui;
::

but any bus will do, and any effects:

code::
c = FxChain(\verb, bus: 16, numChannels: 2);
c.add(ParaEQ.new);
c.add(Compressor.new);
::

subsection:: Where it sits

The group is built after the default group when the server comes up and again
after cmd + period, so the chain hears everything that plays, and whatever reads
the bus at the tail of the root node - ServerPanel's meters, a recorder, Insight -
hears the chain. The server's own volume synth is made after the default group
too, and later, so it lands before the chain: the volume knob is a trim into the
chain rather than a fader after it.

An effect that is off has no node. An effect's node goes after the node of the
effect before it, so the order of link::#-units:: is the order on the bus; and
that node exists exactly when the effect is on, the chain is on and the server is
up - the one thing this class has to get right.

subsection:: Presets

The whole chain writes to one file and reads it back, effect by effect, so a
master setting travels as one thing. The folder is next to the class files and
ignored by git.

code::
c.savePreset("tonight");         // -> <sc EQ>/presets/tonight.scd
c.loadPreset("tonight");
FxChain.presetNames;
::

A preset entry lands on the effect of the same class at that position, on the
first effect of that class otherwise, and makes a new one when there is none and
the class is installed. A class that is not installed is skipped and named.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
A chain under a name. Making another under a taken name frees the old one first.

ARGUMENT:: name
ARGUMENT:: bus
An index, a link::Classes/Bus::, or a BusManager name.
ARGUMENT:: numChannels
ARGUMENT:: server
ARGUMENT:: target
ARGUMENT:: addAction
Where the group goes; after the default group by default. A function answering
a node is evaluated at tree time.

METHOD:: master
The chain on a server's main out, made the first time it is asked for, with a
link::Classes/ParaEQ:: and - when that extension is installed - a
link::Classes/Compressor:: in it, both off. One per server.

METHOD:: at
METHOD:: names
METHOD:: freeAll
The registry.

METHOD:: presetDir
METHOD:: presetPath
METHOD:: presets
METHOD:: presetNames
The preset folder and what is in it, newest first.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: add
Put an effect in the chain, at the end or at code::index::. It leaves whatever it
was doing before and takes this chain's bus and channel count.

METHOD:: remove
Take one out; its node is faded away.

METHOD:: units
The effects, in order on the bus.

METHOD:: at
METHOD:: size

METHOD:: eq
METHOD:: compressor
The first effect of that class, or nil.

METHOD:: unitOfClass

METHOD:: moveUnit
Move one effect to another position. The nodes are moved, not rebuilt.

METHOD:: enabled
The chain as a whole: off, every node is faded out and the bus is left alone,
whatever each effect says for itself.

METHOD:: group
The group on the server, or nil while it is down.

METHOD:: name
METHOD:: server
METHOD:: bus
METHOD:: numChannels

METHOD:: savePreset
METHOD:: loadPreset
METHOD:: presetName
METHOD:: presetFile
METHOD:: asDict
METHOD:: fromDict
The whole chain as one preset - see above.

METHOD:: gui
METHOD:: closeGui
METHOD:: panel
A window - link::Classes/FxChainGUI:: - opened or closed, or the same as a
view. The window is made once and brought to the front after that, and both
ways round announce code::\gui::, so a button elsewhere that opens it -
ServerPanel's code::fx:: - can keep its light right without asking.

METHOD:: analysisPlacement
Where an analyser reading the whole chain goes: the tail of its group.

METHOD:: free
Removes the hooks, drops the nodes and the group, lets the units go.

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;
{ Out.ar(0, PinkNoise.ar(0.1) ! 2) }.play;

c = FxChain.master;
c.gui;
c.eq.enabled = true;
c.eq.preset = \telephone;       // heard on the noise
c.eq.preset = \flat;
c.compressor !? { |k| k.enabled = true; k.threshold = -30; k.ratio = 8 };
c.savePreset("noise test");
c.enabled = false;               // the whole chain out
c.enabled = true;
c.free;
::
